{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED at exact head 0980309a1269e13632263f2a65aaae45e43574e7 (one docs-only commit atop main c43e7b3: notes/2026-08-31-url-reputation-stage-1-decisions.md). Clean worktree: go vet OK, go test 14 ok, go test -race 14 ok. THE NOTE IS STRONG and resolves OQ1-OQ6 of the merged loopback note with concrete, engine-consistent decisions: one normalizer with READ+WRITES as sole writer of url_observations/url_exclusions/url_verdicts and one fold writing url_pipeline_counts is admitted by the DDL grammar (normalizer READ/WRITES optional, EMITS required) and keeps every table single-writer; due-query freshness via caller-supplied now_unix_nano preserves deterministic interpretation (query --param exists); the three OTLP families echo observed_full so scrubbed lookups rejoin exact local observations without a side cache; retention/reset and tombstone posture are explicit; egress scrubbing is on by default with a documented precision cost and no query-sending mode; credentials env-only and scrubbed from failure reports; no RuntimeID/engine change. The two operator decisions are correctly presented as ratification options with recommended defaults (narrow adapter; Web Risk Lookup default, Safe Browsing only for confirmed non-commercial use, VirusTotal only under Premium) - I independently verified the cited API facts today: Safe Browsing v5 urls.search caps requests at 50 URLs, returns cacheDuration, and permits client extension of threat-free results to at most 24 hours; Web Risk Lookup is one URL per request with expireTime and no client canonicalization requirement. ONE REQUIRED CHANGE: R1 the plan has no deliverable for the capture adapter it recommends. Stage 2 builds the Tailapp, stage 3 the companion, stage 4 docs; stage 3 only says keep the capture adapter separately deployable. The merged note OQ1 asked where the adapter lives and who maintains it, and this note answers neither, so as staged the feature ships with no producer of tailapp.url.observed and the end-to-end test in stage 3 would exercise synthetic observations only. Add a concrete reference adapter deliverable: name the mechanism (for Claude Code the natural one is a PostToolUse hook on WebFetch/WebSearch emitting one OTLP/HTTP log record with tailapp.url.observed_full/host to the resident; state the Codex/OpenCode equivalents or mark them unknown), its home (scripts/url-capture/ or beside the companion), its stage (stage 3 with the companion, or a stage 2b), its tests (hook input -\u003e emitted record -\u003e normalized url_observations row), and its maintenance stance; keep the broad harness detail gate as the documented bootstrap alternative. ADVISORIES (non-blocking, fold into the plan or explain): A1 dedupe by checked_full within a companion run so many observed URLs that scrub to one outbound URL cost one provider lookup and fan out one reputation record per observation. A2 upserting the built-in exclusion rows on every recognized pipeline event is wasteful; READ url_exclusions in the normalizer and upsert only when absent, or seed once at first event. A3 reset discards operator exclusions with observations; a separate tiny exclusions Tailapp joined at query time via mounts would let operators reset observations without losing policy - optional, note the trade-off. A4 have the normalizer re-parse observed_full and refuse records whose tailapp.url.host disagrees with the parsed host, so the adapter cannot desynchronize exclusions. A5 the Web Risk row says server-side canonicalization; the docs say the URL need not be canonicalized - reword to avoid implying the client may skip scrubbing. Re-request at the corrected head; the ratification gate items 1-3 go to the operator and I will relay them.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:994c63b45a97e99c4cd130395651e9eacafa274c","head":"0980309a1269e13632263f2a65aaae45e43574e7","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8